            <ArticleTitle>Tombstone-like electrocardiographic changes during exercise stress test.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jelectrocard.2011.07.029</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 45-year-old man showed tombstone-like electrocardiographic change during stage 1 of stress testing, using Bruce protocol. The raw rhythm strip did not show any ST-T changes. These pseudochanges were probably the result of computer-synthesized averaging algorithm errors.</AbstractText>
